Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:06:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(grade): add id_utilisateur_saisie FK on NOTE (MCD fix #3)

Step 4/N of aligning with the corrected MCD. NOTE had no link to the user
who entered it - the MCD's UTILISATEUR ||--o{ NOTE : saisit relationship
had no matching FK.

- New migration V42_27: adds nullable entered_by_user_id FK on grade,
  referencing users(id). Left nullable since existing rows can't be
  honestly backfilled (this wasn't tracked before) - every grade entered
  from now on will always have it set.
- Grade entity: added enteredByUserId field.
- GradeResponse/GradeMapper: expose it.
- GradeService.create() now takes an explicit currentUserId param, mirroring
  the pattern already established in update() (connected user resolved at
  the controller boundary via @AuthenticationPrincipal User, not trusted
  from the request body).
- GradeController.create() wires the connected user through.
- GradeServiceTest updated for the new parameter, asserts enteredByUserId is
  correctly stored.
